{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161673-looking-for-some-help-to-build-a-constantine-esque-laughing-magicians-legacy","id":1161673,"title":"Looking for some help to build a Constantine-esque \"Laughing Magicians\" legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-22T18:17:12-08:00","id":1161673,"title":"Looking for some help to build a Constantine-esque \"Laughing Magicians\" legacy","content":"First off, for those unaware, the Laughing Magicians are something from Vertigo Comic's Hellblazer, and they're premise is a bloodline of people that can do something called Synchronicity Wave Travelling (basically riding the whims of chance and fate to wherever the plot needs them to be.) and that are very adept at rebuking and outsmarting gods from all mythologies and religion. Supposedly existed during the growth of mankind, They rebuke gods and demons other people worship. Some even go so far as to kill or enslave them.<br /> <br /> Okay, so with that out of the way, help is an understatement as in many ways I'm asking for handouts here. Don't get me wrong, I have a lot of ideas bouncing around in my head for flavor, initiation, oblations, etc. It's paring them down to a functional level and properly codifying them that is an issue for me in the short term. I'm imagining Fate is almost certainly the ruling arcana, but where from there? Oblations/ yantras based on relying on chance instead of conscious though to achieve a goal? Maybe games of chance? Encouraging rebellion or independence or perhaps finding loopholes in contracts? Breaking them? This is meant to draw on Constantine himself as much as the bloodline stuff, hence those unfamiliar with him will probably be confused by some of these suggestions.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry that this is all so vague, I'm not the best at this sort of freeform creation. The attainment themselves are another story entirely that will probably be difficult, but in the short term I think just laying out the prerequisites, initiation, and yantra and oblations would be a framework to work with. <br /> <br /> As I said, I'm really coming into this half cocked and asking for handouts, but I'm interested in seeing what your thoughts and ideas are, and I appreciate what you can give. Maybe after this thread I can put somethiby together to show off <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":". 11-22-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T08:32:34-08:00","id":1162468,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Just a couple of thoughts I had (I know you probably already thought about those, but it helps me to outline things in my own head)</div> <br /> <b>Parent Path: </b><br /> Since both the Shadow and the Astral contain entities that could be seen as deities or demons, I could see this Legacy as either Fate/Spirits or Fate/Mind. So we'd have to choose between:<br /> a) Acanthus with Spirits (Time, Fate, Spirits)<br /> b) Mastigos with Fate (Mind, Space, Fate)<br /> <br /> I'd lean towards the second option. The theme of &quot;rebuking gods, so we find our own ways to deal with the forces of the universe&quot; sounds very Mastigos to me. The Demons who plague John could easily be seen as Goetia touched by the Inferno. There's also the fact that Joanna Constantine, her Ancestor, dealt with one of the Endless (Morpheus, AKA Dream): and to me, the status of the Endless (not gods, but concepts subsuming them) is clearly depicted by the Aeons from the Anima Mundi,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites (Initiation); </b>Fate 2, Occult 2 and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher: <i> Academics</i> (if your enemies' powers weaknesses stem from mythology and beleifs, you'd better sit and learn the damn thing), <i>Larceny </i>(their legendary talents for escape), <i>Persuasion</i> (that alows them to convert others to their beliefs, or to outwit gods used to bargain with clueless humans), <i>Investigation</i> (to reflect the whole detective thing), <i>Politics</i> (almost every early Laughing magician was involved with it: I mean, they have an Emperor of Rome amongst their numbers !)<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Initiation. Optional Mind 1.<br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b>Fate 2, Occult 3. Optional Mind 2.<br /> <b>Third Attainment: </b>Fate 3, increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements. Optional Mind 3<br /> <b>Fourth Attainement:</b> Fate 4, Occult 4. Optional Mind 4<br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b> Fate 5, increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain three dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list. Optional Mind 5 <br /> <b>History:</b><br /> The Laughing Magicians would probably be the direst rivals of the Keepers of the Covenant. The Keepers try to ensure the best relationships between mortals and spirits: the Laughing Magicians try to get rid of the spirits. The Keepers have been persecuted by monotheism and resent that period, while the emperor Constantine was the one to legalize Christianit in the first place, to thwart the very same pagan gods the Keepers have sworn to side with. So we'd have two Legacies, with overly similar tools (mastery over Fate, and control over inhuman entities), but radically diverging ethos and a two-millenia old grudge. Ooooh, how I'd like to see them interact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T11:35:40-08:00","id":1162757,"title":"","content":"Also, here's a Tumblr fanpage referencing all use of spells or occult symbols by Constantine, both in the comic and in the recent serie (even though I don't like the serie, it might be helpful). <a href=\"https://john-constantines-spells.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://john-constantines-spells.tumblr.com/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 11-26-2017, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T13:33:20-08:00","id":1162783,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that's awesome. I had been considering the parent path, and I agree Mastigos with Fate is probably most fitting. I think perhaps subterfuge over persuasion might be a better fit for the standard bluff, bluster and misdirection and outfitting, but It's not quite perfect. I'll try and put a post up with a rough outline of ideas when I get home <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The ideas presented here so far are helpful though, so thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T15:12:21-08:00","id":1162804,"title":"","content":"Fate is Primary, right? Some spells that may be useful and thematic as Attainments:<br /> <br /> \u2022: Any of them, really.<br /> \u2022\u2022: Shifting the Odds (so fitting), Warding Gesture (more protective vs other forces interfering with them).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Superlative Luck (just generally useful), Sworn Oaths (seems fitting, binding other beings in magical promises), Shared Fate (this seems like a fitting, tricksy spell to use).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Chaos Mastery (not that fitting, but an awesome, flexible spell, regardless), Strings of Fate (odd &quot;coincidences&quot; for-the-win), <i>Sever Oaths</i> (this is perhaps the most fitting in theme, being able to say &quot;nope&quot; to previous binding laws and vows).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Forge Destiny (on-call supernatural merits are nice, even if it is restricted to allies), Miracle (bonus Successes, screwing over others rolls, both are fitting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T16:31:31-08:00","id":1162821,"title":"","content":"I think that Serendipity really does make the most sense for the first level ability. Shifting the odds is also extremely appropriate at level 2. Perhaps level 3 would utilize fools rush in with an additional reach instead of a fate 3 ability? I like Superlative luck and Sworn Oaths, but also find that they're not perfect fits so I don't feel beholden to them, and Superlative luck just being constantly available with minimal risk seems distasteful? I might be forgetting something about the spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:20:00-08:00","id":1163373,"title":"","content":"As much as I agree with &quot;Mastigos with Fate&quot;, Mind seems a little out of place for me. Space links better to the Laughing Magicians knack for understanding how things connect and to travel the world through Synchronicity. The very concept of Synchronicity is about relationship between things.<br /> <br /> The very first Attainment should be this travel. The ability of the Magician to be where she's meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:06:40-08:00","id":1163397,"title":"","content":"It'd be more appropriate for it to first be about understanding the relationships between things, and later attainments would cover the travel aspects of it. This is because of the experiential nature of Mage in which first you must experience and incorporate that experience into your understanding before you can gain mastery via that understanding. That's why Knowing and Unveiling are front loaded in the arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T22:37:40-08:00","id":1163484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161673-looking-for-some-help-to-build-a-constantine-esque-laughing-magicians-legacy?p=1163397#post1163397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be more appropriate for it to first be about understanding the relationships between things, and later attainments would cover the travel aspects of it. This is because of the experiential nature of Mage in which first you must experience and incorporate that experience into your understanding before you can gain mastery via that understanding. That's why Knowing and Unveiling are front loaded in the arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it is a Legacy, shouldn't the understanding come from the requisites of entry?<br /> <br /> The traveling aspect is very basic on the Laughing Magicians. Usually they don't even use supernatural means to achieve that. The magic isn't the travel per se, but to arrive where you're fated to, when you're fated to. The journey itself is rather mundane, and even expensive sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:36:19-08:00","id":1163543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161673-looking-for-some-help-to-build-a-constantine-esque-laughing-magicians-legacy?p=1163484#post1163484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it is a Legacy, shouldn't the understanding come from the requisites of entry?<br /> <br /> The traveling aspect is very basic on the Laughing Magicians. Usually they don't even use supernatural means to achieve that. The magic isn't the travel per se, but to arrive where you're fated to, when you're fated to. The journey itself is rather mundane, and even expensive sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The requisites for entry are your qualifications to join the legacy, not for performing its functions. <br /> <br /> That said, you probably could make it the first attainment by modeling it off of Red Light/Green Light from Time 1, but using Fate instead as an always on effect. It\u2019s a largely symbolic gesture though as it\u2019s a narrative effect with no real mechanical impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}